{{Quote|Sorry, Artoo, but I've never jumped into the Deep Core before. It's crowded in there and things move fast and this isn't a well-established route yet, so I think an abundance of caution is warranted.|Luke Skywalker, to [[R2-D2]]|<ref name="Heir" />}}
The '''Deep Core''', sometimes referred to as the '''Core of the Galaxy''', was a brightly lit region of [[the galaxy]] that lay at its very [[heart]].<ref name="Heir" /> Despite the presence of important [[Ecumenopolis|city-worlds]] such as [[Troithe]], Byss, and [[Empress Teta]],<ref name="Shadow Fall" /><ref name="Nexus of Power" /> much of the Deep Core was a thinly populated<ref name="VE">''[[Star Wars: The Visual Encyclopedia]]''</ref> and densely packed mass of [[star]]s and [[planet]]s, dangerous to navigate and largely left alone by galactic explorers.<ref name="Heir" /> At its center existed<ref name="Twilight Company">''[[Battlefront: Twilight Company]]''</ref> the [[Galactic Centre]],<ref name="Falcon 36">{{BuildFalconCite|36|Guide to the Galaxy}}</ref> an ancient, supermassive [[black hole]] that bound the galaxy together.<ref name="Twilight Company" /> Traveling towards the Core and away from the [[Galactic Rim|galactic rim]] was referred to as going "coreward."<ref name="Rebel Files">''[[Star Wars: The Rebel Files]]''</ref>

==History==
[[Troithe]], an [[ecumenopolis]] world in the Deep Core's [[Cerberon system]], was once considered a rival to [[Coruscant]] as the cosmopolitan jewel of the [[Galactic Republic]]. However, its location in the Deep Core made it ill-positioned for the Republic's expansion into the [[Colonies]] and the [[Inner Rim Territories|Inner Rim]], causing the world's decline as an industrial powerhouse in the Republic.<ref name="Shadow Fall" />

[[File:DeepCore-TFABG.png|thumb|left|300px|The Deep Core]]
Some [[Jedi]] scholars made the case that the Deep Core planet [[Tython]] was the site of the [[Jedi Order]]'s [[First Jedi Temple|first temple]].<ref name="CL">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref> The [[Mining Guild]] stronghold of [[Empress Teta]] in the Deep Core sided with the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] during the [[Clone Wars]]. Republic-loyal nobles fled to Coruscant.<ref name="Nexus of Power"/> Troithe was subject to [[Incursions against Troithe|Separatist incursions]] during the Clone Wars.<ref name="Shadow Fall" /> With the transition of the Republic into the [[Galactic Empire]] at the war's end, the Empire would take control of Empress Teta, with the now-Imperial-backed nobles arriving on planet and assuming control.<ref name="Nexus of Power" /> The Empire enjoyed support from Troithe.<ref name="Shadow Fall" />

By the [[14 BBY|fifth]] [[Standard year|year]] of [[Galactic Emperor|Emperor]] [[Darth Sidious|Sheev Palpatine's]] reign, the Empire controlled a part of that region referred to as the [[Deep Core Security Zone]]. [[Kren Blista-Vanee]], a member of Palpatine's [[Imperial Ruling Council]], had been instrumental to the creation of [[hyperspace]] [[Hyperspace route|routes]] into the [[star system]]s of the Deep Core.<ref name="Trkn">[[Tarkin (novel)|''Tarkin'']]</ref> It was considered a sensitive region and access to the zone was restricted by the [[15th Deep Core Reserve Fleet]], operating out of nearby Empress Teta.<ref name="Nexus of Power" /> During the [[Battle of Scarif]], [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance]] member [[Jyn Erso]] mentioned a [[Data-tape|data tape]] labelled as "Deep Core Cartography" while searching for the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star's]] [[Death Star plans|plans]] in the Galactic Empire's [[Scarif vault|data vault]] on [[Scarif]].<ref name="Rogue One novel">[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story (novelization)|''Rogue One: A Star Wars Story'' novelization]]</ref>

Following the [[Battle of Yavin]], [[Luke Skywalker]] and [[Nakari Kelen]] [[Mission to Fex|traveled]] to the Deep Core [[moon]] of [[Fex]] to investigate a biological research [[Starship|ship]] belonging to [[Kelen Biolabs]] that had suddenly gone silent.<ref name="Heir" />

During the [[Galactic Civil War]], the archaeologist [[Doctor]] [[Chelli Lona Aphra]] led [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]] to Tython's [[Meridional Ice Cap]] in an attempt to prevent the [[Sith Lord]] from uncovering the true location of the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance's]] [[Echo Base|base]] on [[Hoth]].<ref name="Doctor Aphra 40">[[Doctor Aphra (2016) 40|''Doctor Aphra'' (2016) 40]]</ref>

{{Sec-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
The Deep Core region originates in [[Star Wars Legends|Legends]] continuity and first appeared in the comic ''[[Star Wars: Dark Empire]]'', which ran from 1991 to 1992. It became part of [[canon]] when it was mentioned in the 2014 novel ''[[Tarkin (novel)|Tarkin]]''.

In the game ''[[Star Wars: Jedi Challenges]]'', the Deep Core is referred to as the Core of the Galaxy. The game describes it as a mysterious place in the center of the galaxy, where a challenge awaited those who ventured there.

